.TH FATHOM_AMBIENT 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-ambient \- The glance pane for the terminal beside the agent: latest episode, queue, index, one reason (`reco\-8bx`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom ambient\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-once\fR] [\fB\-\-plain\fR] [\fB\-\-interval\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-deadline\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-index\fR] [\fB\-\-chunk\-units\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR] [\fB\-\-self\-check\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
The glance pane for the terminal beside the agent: latest episode, queue, index, one reason (`reco\-8bx`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR [default: .]
The repository to read
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the pane as one JSON object per change (machine contract `fathom.cli.ambient/1`)
.TP
\fB\-\-once\fR
Print the pane once and exit; never take the screen
.TP
\fB\-\-plain\fR
Draw the pane as text with no terminal taken (ADR\-006 §6.7)
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\-ms\fR \fI<INTERVAL_MS>\fR [default: 400]
How often to look, in milliseconds. 400 is what meets the "under a second" promise at near\-zero cost
.TP
\fB\-\-deadline\fR \fI<DEADLINE>\fR
Stop after this many seconds
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-index\fR
Never index from the pane: read whatever the last index run left, whoever ran it
.TP
\fB\-\-chunk\-units\fR \fI<CHUNK_UNITS>\fR [default: 200]
Episodes to index per slice when this pane is the one keeping the index current
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<WIDTH>\fR
Render at this width instead of the terminal\*(Aqs — for a pipe, a test, or a tmux status line
.TP
\fB\-\-self\-check\fR
Run to the deadline and print what the pane cost: polls, redraws and this process\*(Aqs own CPU share. Exits `11` if it blew the budget of 1 % of a core
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
